Subject: [PATCH] ios: gate GIR sources when introspection is disabled

The iOS cross build configures gnome-desktop with -Dintrospection=false.
gnome-desktop 44.1 still references libgnome_desktop_base_gir from dependency
source lists and calls gnome.generate_gir() unconditionally in the gnome-bg and
gnome-rr subdirectories. With introspection disabled, those variables are not
defined and Meson aborts before building the libraries.

Keep the library builds intact, but make the GIR source variables empty when
introspection is disabled.
--- a/libgnome-desktop/gnome-bg/meson.build
+++ b/libgnome-desktop/gnome-bg/meson.build
@@ -42,0 +43 @@
+if get_option('introspection') # X11IOS_GIR_GATED
@@ -53,0 +55,3 @@
+else
+libgnome_bg_gir = []
+endif
--- a/libgnome-desktop/gnome-rr/meson.build
+++ b/libgnome-desktop/gnome-rr/meson.build
@@ -46,0 +47 @@
+if get_option('introspection') # X11IOS_GIR_GATED
@@ -57,0 +59,3 @@
+else
+libgnome_rr_gir = []
+endif
--- a/libgnome-desktop/meson.build
+++ b/libgnome-desktop/meson.build
@@ -158 +157,0 @@
-      libgnome_desktop_base_gir,
